+# Incidents brief: August and September 2026
+
+Statuses from on-call meeting notes to 30 September; "open" means no record of completion.
+
+## 11 August: ingest stall and full disk
+
+**Impact:** customers saw stale dashboards for about 2.5 hours overnight; no data lost. **Cause:** one malformed batch jammed ingest; its retry logs filled the database disk. **Fix:** restarted ingest without the bad batch, then freed disk space.
+
+Follow-ups:
+
+- Stop bad batches jamming ingest: Jonas, open.
+- 80% disk alert: no owner, open (disk found at 85% by hand in September).
+- 15-minute escalation to the next person: Elif and Sunil, done.
+- Handbook check for the old 30-minute rule: Mara, open.
+
+## 21 September: expired API certificate
+
+**Impact:** public API unreachable for nearly all clients for 47 minutes. **Cause:** the certificate expired; automatic renewal had failed silently all month on an outdated credential. **Fix:** renewed the certificate and restarted the API.
+
+Follow-ups:
+
+- Renewal job repaired, alerts on failure: no owner, done.
+- Calendar reminder 14 days before expiry: no owner, open.
+- Days-until-expiry alert: no owner, open.
+- Expiry check in weekly checklist: no owner, open.
+- Handlers note actions during incidents: everyone, agreed practice.
